      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_only -> detected_only (paper reports surface: not_reported, function: not_reported). Paper (PMID 38985877): \"For surface expression experiments, a FLAG epitope was inserted after K115 in the extracellular domain of AJAP1\". Audit note: Mouse AJAP1 (A2ALI5, 412 aa) has one extra residue upstream, so mouse K115 (LGPK) = human K114 (LVPK); the row already applied this -1 offset. The FLAG construct is only mentioned in methods; surface-expression results for it were not found in the main text (likely supplementary), so surface display is not verified here.] The ledger explicitly names a FLAG epitope inserted after K115 in the extracellular domain of full-length, membrane-anchored AJAP1. The human canonical sequence has K at position 114 (not 115); Python search shows K114 is the only K in the immediate vicinity and the 1-residue offset is consistent with a single indel between mouse and human sequences upstream of this site. The site lies 71 residues from the mature N-terminus and 169 residues from the TM boundary, well within the extracellular domain (44\u2013282). A short ALFA-tag insert here is directly precedented by the published FLAG insertion. Full-length mouse AJAP1 (membrane-anchored) expressed in pCI vector with a FLAG epitope inserted after K115 (mouse numbering) in the extracellular domain, used for surface expression experiments. The paper (PMC11235169) uses mouse AJAP1; human canonical position 114 = K, position 115 = A; mouse K115 maps to human K114 by a 1-residue offset between orthologs. Python search confirmed K114 is the nearest K to the stated position 115 in the human sequence.",
